{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019q6XdpnoMNPLhD9YyyLFmA","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully read all four files. Here's a summary of what you need to understand:\n\n## 1. **SRD097 Requirements (srd097-who.yaml)**\n\nThe SRD defines the following requirements for `cmd/who`:\n\n**R2 - Display Options (R2.1-R2.4):**\n- **R2.1**: `-H` or `--heading` must print a header line\n- **R2.2**: `-u` or `--users` must show idle time (HH:MM, '.' for active <1 min, 'old' for >24 hours)\n- **R2.3**: `-b` or `--boot` must show time of last system boot\n- **R2.4**: `-q` or `--count` must print login names in columns with a count\n\nPlus R1.1-R1.4 (basic functionality) and R3.1-R3.3 (exit codes and SIGPIPE handling).\n\n**Key note**: Must byte-for-byte match GNU who (gwho) via differential testing.\n\n## 2. **cmd/users/main.go** - Reference Pattern\n\nThe `users` command shows the basic utmpx reading pattern:\n- Uses C bindings: `setutxent()`, `getutxent()`, `endutxent()`\n- Filters for `USER_PROCESS` entries\n- Extracts user names from `ut_user`\n- Calls `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for graceful pipe handling\n- Simple argument parsing for optional FILE parameter\n\n## 3. **cmd/pinky/main.go** - Advanced Pattern\n\nThe `pinky` command demonstrates more complex utmpx handling:\n- Reads `ut_type`, `ut_user`, `ut_line`, `ut_host`, `ut_tv.tv_sec`\n- Calculates idle time via `sys.Stat()` and `time.Since(fi.AccessTime)`\n- Parses flag bundles (e.g., `-lfb`)\n- Formats login time using `time.Unix()`\n- Handles passwd lookups for detailed user info\n\n## 4. **cmd/who/main.go** - Current State\n\nThe file **already exists** but is **incomplete**. It currently implements:\n- **Done**: R1.1-R1.4 (basic user listing, FILE argument, \"who am i\", error handling)\n- **Missing**: R2.1-R2.4 (all display options: `-H`, `-u`, `-b`, `-q`)\n\nThe existing code has the foundation in place:\n- Proper utmpx reading via C bindings\n- Entry structure with user, line, time, host\n- Print formatting infrastructure\n- Argument parsing framework that needs expansion for option flags\n\nThe implementation needs to extend `parseArgs()` to handle `-H`, `-u`, `-b`, `-q` flags and add corresponding functions to display headers, idle times, boot times, and user counts."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44efa1bf-5dfc-4bcb-b29a-a970794915e8","uuid":"616887c4-3668-4193-9745-b092d6d8f6cc","timestamp":"2026-05-27T14:23:05.742Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to read three files from this Go project to understand the requirements and patterns for implementing `cmd/who/main.go`. Please read these files completely and return their full contents:\n\n1. `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd097-who.yaml` — the SRD with requirements R2.1-R2.4\n2. `cmd/users/main.go` — existing utmpx reading pattern\n3. `cmd/pinky/main.go` — existing utmpx reading pattern\n4. `cmd/who/main.go` — check if it exists already\n\nThe working directory is `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5582`","agentId":"a3772013a02bf4dcc","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully read all four files. Here's a summary of what you need to understand:\n\n## 1. **SRD097 Requirements (srd097-who.yaml)**\n\nThe SRD defines the following requirements for `cmd/who`:\n\n**R2 - Display Options (R2.1-R2.4):**\n- **R2.1**: `-H` or `--heading` must print a header line\n- **R2.2**: `-u` or `--users` must show idle time (HH:MM, '.' for active <1 min, 'old' for >24 hours)\n- **R2.3**: `-b` or `--boot` must show time of last system boot\n- **R2.4**: `-q` or `--count` must print login names in columns with a count\n\nPlus R1.1-R1.4 (basic functionality) and R3.1-R3.3 (exit codes and SIGPIPE handling).\n\n**Key note**: Must byte-for-byte match GNU who (gwho) via differential testing.\n\n## 2. **cmd/users/main.go** - Reference Pattern\n\nThe `users` command shows the basic utmpx reading pattern:\n- Uses C bindings: `setutxent()`, `getutxent()`, `endutxent()`\n- Filters for `USER_PROCESS` entries\n- Extracts user names from `ut_user`\n- Calls `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for graceful pipe handling\n- Simple argument parsing for optional FILE parameter\n\n## 3. **cmd/pinky/main.go** - Advanced Pattern\n\nThe `pinky` command demonstrates more complex utmpx handling:\n- Reads `ut_type`, `ut_user`, `ut_line`, `ut_host`, `ut_tv.tv_sec`\n- Calculates idle time via `sys.Stat()` and `time.Since(fi.AccessTime)`\n- Parses flag bundles (e.g., `-lfb`)\n- Formats login time using `time.Unix()`\n- Handles passwd lookups for detailed user info\n\n## 4. **cmd/who/main.go** - Current State\n\nThe file **already exists** but is **incomplete**. It currently implements:\n- **Done**: R1.1-R1.4 (basic user listing, FILE argument, \"who am i\", error handling)\n- **Missing**: R2.1-R2.4 (all display options: `-H`, `-u`, `-b`, `-q`)\n\nThe existing code has the foundation in place:\n- Proper utmpx reading via C bindings\n- Entry structure with user, line, time, host\n- Print formatting infrastructure\n- Argument parsing framework that needs expansion for option flags\n\nThe implementation needs to extend `parseArgs()` to handle `-H`, `-u`, `-b`, `-q` flags and add corresponding functions to display headers, idle times, boot times, and user counts."}],"totalDurationMs":11028,"totalTokens":25791,"totalToolUseCount":4,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8910,"cache_read_input_tokens":16180,"output_tokens":694,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8910},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":7,"output_tokens":694,"cache_read_input_tokens":16180,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8910,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"messag